What opEntryT Is

SEQ 330 A1 (Tony, 2026-10-09): a name matches as an operator only if it is an ENTRY of the
Operators registry, never the registry itself; a name followed by a call is the call's target.
pop.sh runs this fixture WITH THE SWITCH ON. OE-R names the registry bare and reads its length:
before A1 the candidate took Operators for a prefix operator, refused it by name, and the refusal
ended oeShow, so neither row printed. OE-E is the control: an entry (+) is still an operator.
The call clause is pinned by the fleet's generated-parse rows (Token's body ends Operators()).
